From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:49:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] runtime(#821): write runtime-config.json through an
 exclusive per-writer temporary [skip ci]

AgentMemory.open writes the packaged default runtime-config.json when a store
has none. It wrote through one shared .runtime-config.json.tmp opened with
truncation, the pattern R-1 found in the generation witness. On e88bced2:
- two openers of a new store could truncate each other's inode; a crash in
  between published an empty configuration, and every later open refused
  (runtime configuration is not valid JSON);
- a symlink planted at that name was followed, overwriting a file outside the
  store, and the configuration became the symlink;
- a FIFO planted there blocked the first open.

_atomic_write_text now creates .runtime-config.json.<pid>.<random>.tmp with
O_CREAT|O_EXCL (mode 0o666 less umask, as before). It keeps write, fsync and
os.replace, and on any failure before the rename closes its descriptor and
removes only its own temporary.

tests/test_821_runtime_config_temporary.py adds 7 tests. The race, symlink,
FIFO and failure-hygiene tests fail on e88bced2 (6 of 7) and pass here (7/7,
3 runs).

